      "value": "@{627e94e69bf04e1ede28a21b|full_name}\nWhen I am operating Main Menu with both hands, I feel this behavior is strange.\nThis is because only one pointer is actually active at any time, even though both pointers are on Main Menu.\nThis causes confusion when scrolling horizontally. (If the active pointer is not on the menu, we cannot even scroll vertically.)\nMarking this Canny as `NOT A BUG` can be interpreted as assuming that Main Menu is operated with only one hand.\nIn that case, you should not display the pointer on both.\nLike anatawa12 created this Canny, Scrolling based on the pointer of the tilted stick is intuitive. But now, it is not.\nYou can see that this behavior has caused inconveniences before, such as Canny below.\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1137-thumbstick-scrolling-only-works-if-you-open-the-quick-menu-with-the-left-ha\nThis is not just a problem with Main Menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
